export const CURSOR_RULES =
  '# Volt UI (Angular)\n\n- Volt first: reuse an existing atom before hand-building UI; never import `ng-primitives` to bypass Volt.\n- The `volt-ui` MCP server is the source of exact selectors, inputs, status and examples (`find_components`, `get_component`, `get_usage_example`); never invent an input.\n- Match the project\'s mode: package (`Volt*`, `\'@voltui/components\'`) or copy (`Ui*`, `./ui`).\n\nMCP server `volt-ui` (https://voltui.dev/api/mcp): `list_components`, `find_components`, `get_component`, `get_usage_example`, `get_theme_info`, `generate_cli_command`.\n\n## Playbooks\n\n### adoption\n- Before writing UI, check whether Volt already owns the responsibility (MCP `find_components`); reuse the atom and keep layout, copy and domain logic in the app.\n- Never rebuild Button, Card, Input, Badge, Alert, Tabs or an overlay with raw Tailwind, and never import `ng-primitives` in an app that consumes Volt.\n- Native HTML is right only where Volt has no equivalent or the native element is the point (route-backed tab strips are real anchors). If Volt cannot do something, say so instead of working around it silently.\n\n### component-selection\n- Action that changes state → Button; navigation → `<a voltButton routerLink>`; never a button inside a link.\n- Fixed short list → NativeSelect; custom options/groups → Select; searchable or remote → Combobox (`filterMode="manual"`, the app owns the request).\n- Form value / consent → Checkbox; immediate setting → Switch; tool pressed state → Toggle/ToggleGroup.\n- Decision that blocks → Dialog; secondary panel → Drawer; anchored contextual content → Popover; hint → Tooltip (never the only copy).\n- Persistent page feedback → Alert; transient confirmation → Toast; unknown wait → Spinner; known layout → Skeleton.\n\n### distribution\n- Detect the mode first: `@voltui/components` (package: `Volt*`, `volt-*`) or a copied `ui/` folder (copy: `Ui*`, `ui-*`). Never mix them; `\'volt\'` is not importable in a consumer.\n- Copy mode: `npx @voltui/cli add <name>`; package mode: `npm install @voltui/components`.\n- Pass the project\'s mode (`package` | `copy`) to the MCP tools to get matching selectors and imports.\n\n### forms\n- Wrap controls in FormField (label, hint, error); show errors after `touched && invalid`, as visible text.\n- Volt controls are ControlValueAccessors: use `[formControl]`/`ngModel` directly; a literal `value="a"` is an initial value, not a lock.\n- `disabled` leaves the tab order; `aria-disabled` on a `voltButton` keeps focus but you must guard the handler.\n- Server search: Combobox `filterMode="manual"`, `(queryChange)` is what was typed, debounce and let the latest response win, pass results as returned, set `[loading]`.\n\n### overlays\n- Dialog: trigger-driven `[voltDialog]`, controlled `voltDialogRoot [(open)]`, or `VoltDialogService`; always title + description; `[dismissible]="false"` while a request is pending.\n- Destructive confirm → `role="alertdialog"` with initial focus on the safe action. Focus is trapped and returns to the trigger; do not manage it by hand.\n- Overlays are an attribute directive on a real `<button>` plus an `<ng-template>`. Never import `Ngp*`.\n- Toast is transient confirmation; Alert is persistent page feedback.\n\n### styling\n- Prefer variants/sizes, then the theme, then `class` on the component (merged with tailwind-merge, so it replaces defaults), then a layout wrapper. Do not rewrite a component.\n- Use semantic utilities (`bg-primary`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`), never hard-coded colours or `bg-[var(--x)]`.\n- Presets: colour `volt|ember|sage|dusk|glacier`, style `sharp|soft|brutal|ghost|retro`; dark mode is a class on `<html>`.\n- Pressed/selected/checked states must be visibly distinct and contrast-checked; colour alone is not meaning.\n';

